# Pico Website - Cursor Rules

## Overview
This is the marketing website for Pico, a maker of privacy-first AI apps for Apple
Silicon. The site is a single-page Jekyll site hosted on GitHub Pages at picogpt.app.

Products featured on the home page:
- Pico AI Server — local LLM server (Mac App Store id6738607769)
- Pico Flux — on-device AI image generation (Mac App Store id6725615977)
- Pico Studio — native AI assistant, "Coming soon" (current version id1668205047)

## File Structure
- `index.html` — single-page home (hero, app sections, blog teaser, community)
- `_layouts/default.html` — shared shell: <head>, sticky nav, footer
- `_layouts/page.html` — wrapper for legal pages (inherits default)
- `_layouts/post.html` — blog post layout (inherits default)
- `_includes/check.svg` — checkmark icon used in feature lists
- `blog/index.html` — blog index
- `_posts/[year]/[month]/[date]-[slug].md` — blog posts
- `privacy-policy.html`, `terms-of-use.html` — legal pages (use `layout: page`)
- `assets/css/input.css` / `main.css` — Tailwind source / compiled output
- `tailwind.config.js`, `package.json` — CSS build tooling (not deployed)
- `LLMs.txt` — machine-readable site/product summary

## Design System
- Light, Apple-style aesthetic. Tailwind CSS, compiled to a static stylesheet.
- Custom colors (see `tailwind.config.js`):
  ink #1d1d1f, subtle #6e6e73, hairline #d2d2d7, mist #f5f5f7. Accent blue #0071e3.
- System font stack (-apple-system / Inter). Generous spacing, rounded corners.

## CSS Build (IMPORTANT)
Tailwind is precompiled to `assets/css/main.css` — there is no runtime CDN.
GitHub Pages does NOT rebuild the CSS, so the compiled file must be committed.

After editing any HTML/markup (new Tailwind classes), regenerate the CSS:
1. One-time: `npm install`
2. Build: `npm run build:css`  (or `npm run watch:css` while developing)
3. Commit the updated `assets/css/main.css`.

- `assets/css/input.css` — Tailwind directives + custom CSS (source, not served)
- `assets/css/main.css` — compiled, minified output (served + committed)
- `tailwind.config.js` — theme + content globs; scans `*.html`, `_layouts`,
  `_includes`, `blog`, `_posts`. New files outside these globs need a glob added.

## Blog Post Management
When adding a new blog post:
1. Create the post in `_posts/[year]/[month]/[date]-[slug].md` with front matter
   `layout: post`, `title`, `date`, and a descriptive `excerpt` (1-2 sentences).
2. The home page blog teaser and the blog index update automatically — they read
   `site.posts` via Liquid, so no manual homepage edit is needed.
3. Optionally refresh the "From the blog" wording in `index.html` if the focus shifts.

## Jekyll Configuration
- Permalink structure: `/blog/:title/`
- Use kramdown for markdown processing
- Posts use the `post` layout; legal pages use the `page` layout

## Notes
- Real App Store icons: `icon.png` is the Pico AI Server icon. Pico Flux and Pico
  Studio currently use styled placeholder tiles in `index.html` — swap in real icons
  at `/assets/images/products/flux.png` and `/studio.png` when available.
- Keep links to Docs (pico-1.gitbook.io/homelab), Discord, and GitHub prominent.

## Code Style
- Use proper HTML escaping in Jekyll templates
- Avoid escaped quotes (`\"`) in HTML files
- Keep front matter clean and properly formatted
